 "notes": "AxionPhoton limit from ALP-photon conversion in the Virgo cluster B-field distorting the X-ray spectrum of the M87 nucleus (Chandra). Curve is the M87 95% c.l. exclusion contour (lower boundary of the middle-blue excluded region) from Fig 6 (Bayesian.pdf in e-print), benchmark B0=31.5 uG. Flat low-mass value ~1.45e-12 GeV^-1 matches quoted bound g_agamma<1.49e-12 GeV^-1 (Eq 5.3). Curve rises (weakens) for m_a>~1e-13 eV as conversion is suppressed. Abstract 2.6e-12 is the weakest limit under B-field-model variations (B0=35 uG); we report the headline benchmark contour that the figure plots. Axes log-log, calibrated from decade labels; low-mass first point extended flat to plot edge 1e-14 eV. Not a DM search, so no density dependence.",
